 ## Overview
-The GSP Training Loss is the objective function used to optimize the parameters of 3D Gaussian kernels, including position, opacity, covariance, and material properties, within the Gaussian Splashing (GSP) framework [S1]. It extends the standard color reconstruction loss with normal consistency and anisotropy regularization to prevent artifacts caused by excessive kernel elongation during solid object simulation [S1]. Unlike standard 3D Gaussian Splatting which focuses on static geometry, this loss is designed to maintain geometric stability and physical plausibility in dynamic or physically-based rendering contexts [S1].
