 ## Background
-The GSP Training Loss originates from the Gaussian Splashing framework, which unifies particles for versatile motion synthesis and rendering [S1]. It builds upon the 3D Gaussian Splatting method by incorporating physically-based rendering concepts and position-based dynamics [S1]. The normal consistency term is adapted from GaussianShader [S1]. The velocity distortion loss is introduced in the context of adaptive spatio-temporal 3D Gaussian Splatting for scenes with oscillatory motion [S2].
